			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize RecoverState into dedicated PascalCase modules\n\nDecompose the 177-line `RecoverState.rs` monolith into a directory of focused modules (`ValidateAndCleanState`, `SafeStateOperationWithTimeout`, `RecoverStateWithBackoff`) to enforce the project's `Struct::Struct` and `Fn` naming conventions. The original file contained three distinct recovery primitives: predicate-driven map filtering, off-thread blocking operations with timeout, and async retry with exponential backoff.\n\nThese utilities are now exposed as individual module files with a clear \"one export per file\" identity, aligning with recent architectural shifts seen in `MementoLoader` and `FileRealpath`. The parent file now serves strictly as a barrel export and architectural documentation, clarifying the separation between validation, timeout handling, and backoff logic while awaiting formal integration into the `ApplicationState` recovery flow.",
