				1137,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize MementoLoader into dedicated function modules\n\nDecompose the 190-line `MementoLoader.rs` monolith into a directory of focused PascalCase modules (`LoadInitialMementoFromDisk`, `LoadMementoWithRecovery`, `AttemptMementoRecovery`, `CreateCorruptedBackup`) to enforce the project's `Struct::Struct` and `Fn` naming conventions.\n\nThe original file contained logic for best-effort loading, recovery flows, and timestamped backup creation. These are now exposed as individual module files with a clear \"one export per file\" identity, aligning with the architectural shift seen in recent commits (`RecoverState`). The file itself now serves as a barrel export and architectural documentation, clarifying the separation between the best-effort `default()` loader and the error-propagating recovery loader.\n\nThis change prepares the persistence layer for cleaner dependency injection from `Environment::StorageProvider` and reduces coupling in the `ApplicationState` boot path.",
			"SHA": "600afe5343df30878c1aaea0f8fd7a9b6be7b7fd"
		},
